// Title: Raccine Uninstall
// Sigma ID: a31eeaed-3fd5-478e-a8ba-e62c6b3f9ecc
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-01-21 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects commands that indicate a Raccine removal from an end system. Raccine is a free
//   ransomware protection tool.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate deinstallation by administrative staff
// References:
//   - https://github.com/Neo23x0/Raccine
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_disable_raccine.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "taskkill " and ProcessCommandLine contains "RaccineSettings.exe") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "reg.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "delete" and ProcessCommandLine contains "Raccine Tray") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "schtasks" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/DELETE" and ProcessCommandLine contains "Raccine Rules Updater")
